Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:36:44 +0800
Subject: i2c: hix5hd2: finish a transaction that completes late

On a Hi3716CV200 the interrupt path never finishes a transfer inside
the adapter timeout: the completion expires after 100 jiffies -- 1 s
at HZ=100 -- while the handler still reports I2C_OVER_INTR (SR bit 0)
about 30 ms later, ten times in a row, so the client gets -ETIMEDOUT
for a transaction that in fact completed.

The late delivery has two candidates: a functional clock running far
below the rate the divider was computed from, or a genuinely late
event.

The driver need not choose between them: wait in 10 ms slices against
a fixed 2 s deadline instead of one blocking wait at adap->timeout, so
a late but real completion returns the transaction's own ACK/NACK
rather than -ETIMEDOUT. The timeout path and its error handling are
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)


diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-hix5hd2.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-hix5hd2.c
index 95ab910b80c0..8eb22cf01c0a 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-hix5hd2.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-hix5hd2.c
@@ -327,8 +327,28 @@ static int hix5hd2_i2c_xfer_msg(struct hix5hd2_i2c_priv *priv,
 	reinit_completion(&priv->msg_complete);
 	hix5hd2_i2c_message_start(priv, stop);
 
-	time_left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&priv->msg_complete,
-						priv->adap.timeout);
+	/*
+	 * The event does arrive, only later than the driver is willing to
+	 * wait: on a Hi3716CV200 the handler reported I2C_OVER_INTR (SR bit 0)
+	 * about 30 ms after a 100-jiffies wait -- 1 s at HZ=100 -- had given
+	 * up, ten times in a row.  Why the delivery is late is not settled
+	 * yet; until it is, wait in slices against a fixed 2 s deadline so a
+	 * late but real completion returns the transaction's own ACK/NACK
+	 * rather than -ETIMEDOUT.
+	 */
+	{
+		unsigned long deadline = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(2000);
+		unsigned int slice = 0;
+
+		time_left = 0;
+		while (slice < 200 && time_after(deadline, jiffies)) {
+			time_left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&priv->msg_complete,
+								msecs_to_jiffies(10));
+			if (time_left)
+				break;
+			slice++;
+		}
+	}
 	if (time_left == 0) {
 		priv->state = HIX5I2C_STAT_RW_ERR;
 		priv->err = -ETIMEDOUT;
-- 
